#
# The block spelling's own-key refusal as a `when` GATE: `inner` is a parameterized rule (evaluated only
# through the call, never on its own, so the file's exit and the console lines are the OUTER rule's), and
# over `R1.Cfg` (its own key `Limits` names a member, no member holds a `Limits` of its own) it is refused,
# so `outer`'s condition cannot be evaluated and `outer` fails closed with the refusal, remedy included,
# printed whole on the outer rule's line.
#
rule inner(cfgs) { %cfgs[*] { Limits exists } }
rule outer when inner(Resources.*.Cfg) { Resources exists }
